.Dd October 29, 2026
.Dt MOUNT_MSDOS 8
.Os Minkar
.Sh NAME
.Nm mount_msdos
.Nd mount a FAT file system
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl o Ar options
.Op Fl u Ar user
.Op Fl g Ar group
.Op Fl m Ar mask
.Ar special
.Ar node
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
mounts the FAT12, FAT16 or FAT32 file system on the device
.Ar special
at the directory
.Ar node .
It is usually run by
.Xr mount 8
as
.Ql mount -t msdos .
.Pp
FAT keeps no owner or permissions for its files. All of them take the
owner, group and permissions given by these options, or by default those of
.Ar node ;
with none of
.Fl u ,
.Fl g
and
.Fl m ,
as on macOS, the permissions are 0777 (how
.Xr diskarbitrationd 8
mounts a volume):
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl o Ar options
Options as in
.Xr mount 8 ,
such as
.Cm rdonly
or
.Cm noexec .
.It Fl u Ar user
The owner of the files, a name or a number.
.It Fl g Ar group
The group of the files, a name or a number.
.It Fl m Ar mask
The permissions of the files, in octal.
.El
.Pp
Times are stored in local time on FAT; the kernel converts them with the
time zone in effect when the file system is mounted.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Mount the first partition of a USB disk, owned by user
.Ql minkar :
.Pp
.Dl mount_msdos -u minkar /dev/disk2s1 /Volumes/USB
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mount 2 ,
.Xr fsck_msdos 8 ,
.Xr mount 8 ,
.Xr newfs_msdos 8
